WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:11.058
Hi! Mushrooms grow in the ground, but are they plants? And what's that fuzzy stuff on old bread? Today we'll learn about fungi.

2
00:00:11.208 --> 00:00:16.362
Mushrooms, the mould on bread and the yeast used for baking are all fungi.

3
00:00:16.512 --> 00:00:22.194
Fungi are not plants. They have no green leaves and can't make their own food.

4
00:00:22.344 --> 00:00:28.026
Fungi get food from dead and decaying things, like fallen leaves, wood and old bread.

5
00:00:28.176 --> 00:00:36.018
Fungi reproduce by spores. Spores are tiny and light, and blow to new places.

6
00:00:36.168 --> 00:00:39.306
Fungi like warm, damp places.

7
00:00:39.456 --> 00:00:44.154
In an experiment, damp bread grows mould faster than dry bread.

8
00:00:44.304 --> 00:00:48.234
In the fridge it's cold, so mould grows more slowly.

9
00:00:48.384 --> 00:00:55.458
Fungi break down fallen leaves and dead plants and animals, which keeps nature clean.

10
00:00:55.608 --> 00:01:02.586
Watch out! Mushrooms grow in the ground, so many pupils think they're plants. That's wrong!

11
00:01:02.736 --> 00:01:10.074
Plants have green parts and make their own food. Mushrooms can't. They take food from decaying things.

12
00:01:10.224 --> 00:01:14.922
So mushrooms are fungi, not plants.

13
00:01:15.072 --> 00:01:23.730
Your turn! Which group of living things is bread mould? Pause and think.

14
00:01:23.880 --> 00:01:28.818
Mould is a fungus. Did you get it right?

15
00:01:28.968 --> 00:01:37.218
Another one! How do fungi reproduce? Pause and think.

16
00:01:37.368 --> 00:01:42.954
Fungi reproduce by spores. Did you get it right?

17
00:01:43.104 --> 00:01:52.938
Here's another! Which goes mouldy first, damp bread or dry bread? Pause and think.

18
00:01:53.088 --> 00:02:00.450
Fungi like damp places, so the damp bread goes mouldy first. Did you get it right?

19
00:02:00.600 --> 00:02:08.898
Try one more! Can fungi make their own food? Pause and think.

20
00:02:09.048 --> 00:02:16.314
No. Fungi get food from dead or decaying things. Did you get it right?

21
00:02:16.464 --> 00:02:25.146
Try one more! Why does bread keep longer in the fridge? Pause and think.

22
00:02:25.296 --> 00:02:33.762
It's cold in the fridge, so fungi grow slowly and the bread takes longer to go mouldy. Did you get it right?

23
00:02:33.912 --> 00:02:43.482
Last one! Which group of living things is the yeast used in baking? Pause and think.

24
00:02:43.632 --> 00:02:48.570
Yeast is a fungus. Did you get it right?

25
00:02:48.720 --> 00:02:58.842
Remember: fungi aren't plants. They can't make their own food and feed on decaying things. They reproduce by spores and like warm, damp places.

26
00:02:58.992 --> 00:03:03.882
Never eat wild mushrooms - some are poisonous!

